ay the right card. Final decision: Play the ♥7.\n\n\n", 'output': 'Evaluation: The current play to beat is a single 6, which is a very low card. Looking at my hand, I possess a single 7 (♥7), which is my lowest single card and effectively dead weight since I lack an 8 to form a straight (and 3 Eights have already been played). My hand is otherwise well-structured with a Sequence of Pairs (99-1010-JJ), a Full House (555 with 66), and strong high cards (Q, A, Red Joker).\n\nReason: Playing the ♥7 is the optimal move here. It allows me to shed my lowest, most isolated card while beating the opponent\'s low play. It preserves my strong combinations (Sequence of Pairs and Full House) and keeps my high cards (A, Red Joker) for regaining control later. Passing on a 6 would be a mistake as it is a rare opportunity to play a small single.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♥7"]}'}
